<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Seven Oaks</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1816">1816</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pemmican-war">Pemmican War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Seven Oaks was a clash on 19 June 1816 near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River Colony</a>, in present-day Winnipeg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> led by Cuthbert Grant, allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a>, killed Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-semple">Robert Semple</a> and about twenty men of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a>'s colony, losing one of their own. It was the bloodiest episode of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pemmican-war">Pemmican War</a> and is remembered as a founding moment of Métis national identity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-seven-oaks.jpg" alt="Battle of Seven Oaks" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles William Jefferys · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Fight_at_Seven_Oaks.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
